<div class="sh">Halacha Four &mdash; <em>Bikur Cholim</em> (Visiting the Sick)</div>
<div class="snb">Section 11 of Hilchos Raishis HaGez</div>

<p class="ni">And this is the aspect of <em>bikur cholim</em> [visiting the sick]. For until Yaakov there was no weakness [before death], as our Sages of blessed memory said (Bava Metzia 87). For in truth it is a great good that a person falls ill before his death, as our Sages of blessed memory said there &mdash; for if not, he would not take it to heart to give instructions to his household. It turns out that illness before death is a great good, in order that he should give instructions to his household.</p>

<p>And the essential <em>tzava&rsquo;ah</em> [last testament] is that he instructs his sons and his household after him to guard the way of Hashem &mdash; as all the <em>tzaddikim</em> did who rebuked Yisrael close to their death. It turns out that the <em>tzava&rsquo;ah</em> is the aspect of the illumination of son and student &mdash; illuminating <em>da&rsquo;as</em> in them, that they know Hashem and guard themselves from transgressions, heaven forbid, and walk in the ways of Hashem &mdash; which is the essential illumination of son and student. And this is drawn down even more at the time of the illness of the true <em>tzaddikim</em>, for then they are occupied even more greatly in this, so that their <em>da&rsquo;as</em> should remain after them forever. And as we find with many <em>tzaddikim</em> who revealed lofty things and very great <em>da&rsquo;as</em> at the time of their illness close to their death &mdash; such as Rabbi Eliezer the Great who taught Rabbi Akiva three hundred <em>halachos</em> concerning <em>baheres azah</em> [an intense bright spot] etc., and Rabbeinu HaKadosh [Rabbi Yehudah HaNasi] and Rabbi Shimon bar Yochai, and similarly very many others. For then the <em>Shechinah</em> rests upon him, as our Sages of blessed memory said: the <em>Shechinah</em> is above the head of the sick person. For at the time of his illness a great light is added to him through the spirit from above (<em>ruach dil&rsquo;eila</em>) which begins to descend below, so that the soul departs through this &mdash; as explained in the discourse <em>Vihi Na Pi Shnayim B&rsquo;Ruchecha</em> etc.</p>

<p>And therefore Yaakov precisely merited to effect with Hashem, blessed-be-He, that a person should fall ill before his death, so that he should instruct his sons and they should guard the way of Hashem &mdash; which is the aspect of the illumination of son and student. For Yaakov&rsquo;s bed was complete (<em>mitaso sheleimah</em>) without any blemish &mdash; he only merited children who were all <em>tzaddikim</em>, who would receive his <em>da&rsquo;as</em> from him and bequeath their <em>da&rsquo;as</em> to the generations, to know Hashem &mdash; which is the aspect of the illumination of son and student. For the student is comprised within the son, as mentioned. And Yaakov also had many students, for he would convert converts, as our Sages of blessed memory said. It turns out that Yaakov merited especially to the illumination of son and student, for his bed was complete.</p>

<p>And therefore he was the first who fell ill close to his death, so that he should draw down even more then the illumination of son and student &mdash; which is the essential <em>tzava&rsquo;ah</em>. And this is the essential [purpose] of <em>bikur cholim</em>: to speak with him so that he should attend to his affairs, as our Sages of blessed memory said &mdash; that he should give instructions to his household, as mentioned. That he should warn the members of his household to walk in the ways of Hashem. And he also arranges for them the apportioning of his assets, so that they should not come to strife and robbery, heaven forbid, and transgress the words of Hashem. And therefore he arranges things for them and warns them to fulfil his words and to walk in the ways of Hashem and His commandments.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of <em>vayugad l&rsquo;Yosef leimor hineh avicha choleh vayikach es shnei vanav imo</em> [and it was told to Yosef saying, behold your father is ill, and he took his two sons with him] etc. (Bereishis 48:1). For he went to visit him and took his sons with him so that he should bless them before his death &mdash; that is, so that he should bring <em>da&rsquo;as</em> of Hashem into them before his death, which is the essential blessing. And then <em>vayishtachu Yisrael al rosh hamitah</em> [and Yisrael bowed at the head of the bed] &mdash; for his bed was complete without blemish. And also for <em>Shechinah lemaalah me&rsquo;rashosav</em> [the <em>Shechinah</em> is above his head] etc., as Rashi explains there. For he merited to both: that the <em>Shechinah</em> should be above his head, through which he merits the attainment of the <em>makifin</em> that he draws down from Hashem, blessed-be-He. And he also merited to bring the <em>makifin</em> and <em>da&rsquo;as</em> into his holy sons &mdash; which is the aspect of the complete bed (<em>mitah sheleimah</em>) &mdash; which is the essential completeness of the soul, when one merits to leave one&rsquo;s <em>da&rsquo;as</em> after oneself through righteous and upright sons and students, as mentioned.</p>

<p>And then one does not die at all. For when one&rsquo;s <em>da&rsquo;as</em> remains after oneself, one remains oneself &mdash; for the essential person is the <em>da&rsquo;as</em>, as mentioned. And therefore our Sages of blessed memory said: Yaakov our patriarch did not die &mdash; for since he merited to the complete bed, that is, righteous sons who received his <em>da&rsquo;as</em> from him for the generations, to know Hashem from generation to generation forever &mdash; behold, he is alive and enduring forever and ever, as mentioned. And this is the aspect of <em>Dovid Melech Yisrael chai v&rsquo;kayam</em> [Dovid King of Yisrael is alive and enduring], as mentioned.</p>

